  "distilled_learning": "In Windows PowerShell environments, passing an unquoted ref such as @s8f3k2p9:e1 invokes PowerShell argument splatting, which interprets the token as an in-scope parameter variable rather than a literal string argument. AI agents operating desktop automation CLIs must enforce qualified ref validation (rejecting bare refs like @e8) and format references with explicit single quotes ('@s8f3k2p9:e1'). This defense is enforced in DesktopRefToken.powershell_quoted() and verified in test contracts."
